message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "DRE Linked Data: Linked Open Data publication for Omeka S"
abstract: >-
  An Omeka S module that publishes an Omeka S site as Linked Open Data. Every
  public item, item set and media gets a dereferenceable URI that redirects
  browsers to the record page and RDF clients to Turtle, N-Triples or JSON-LD,
  following the W3C 303 pattern. The RDF is a clean projection of the record
  rather than Omeka's internal JSON-LD: platform bookkeeping is dropped, private
  values and links to private resources never appear, Numeric Data Types values
  become typed XSD literals, and Wikidata, GND and Library of Congress
  identifiers become owl:sameAs or skos:exactMatch links. An admin-triggered job
  writes the whole public graph as gzipped N-Triples for loading into a
  triplestore such as Apache Jena Fuseki, a VoID and DCAT description documents
  the dataset and its linksets, and a page block presents it to visitors. Built
  for the Africa Multiple Cluster of Excellence Digital Research Environment.
